<SiteLayout title="Evidence & reproduction" description="What Ardor Lite's reviewed evidence can establish: archived aggregates, report transcriptions, synthetic demonstrations and explicit historical-replication limits." type="evidence">
<header class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">The evidence policy</span><h1>A result is only as strong<br />as its boundary.</h1><p class="lede">The Indian-equity evidence supports no certified or live strategy. Ardor Lite preserves what was tested, what failed, what remains blocked and what can be reproduced.</p></header>
<div class="prose"><h2>What this snapshot contains</h2><p>The evidence collection contains six cases, 114 catalog records, 204 claim entries, 18 reviewed figure/table relationships, five independent synthetic method demonstrations and four preview lanes.</p><p>The 114 records cover 49 archive-cohort records and 65 other scoped designs, versions and paths. Mechanisms and stages overlap. They are not 114 independent strategy trials, and their count is not a multiple-testing denominator.</p><p>Archive coverage, the 27-family census, 26 current main registrations, 2,716 trial rows and 1,264 accepted Atlas cells have different definitions. They must not be added into a strategy count.</p><h2>Research evidence and explanatory material</h2><p>Historical research, explanatory text, synthetic demonstrations and current-source excerpts have distinct roles. Five Momentum and 23 engineering/Bridge source excerpts have their own capture identities and reserved-rights notices. They explain captured current code; they do not establish exact historical execution or independently reproduce empirical results.</p><p>The <a href="/research/cases/delivery-insider/#delivery-construction-discrepancy">Delivery construction discrepancy</a> retains the archived definition and distinguishes the captured ratio-level predicate, disclosure-date window and unresolved June run identity. Original claims, values and the null conclusion remain unchanged.</p><h2>Four distinct reproduction labels</h2><dl class="record-facts"><dt>Archived result</dt><dd>Recorded aggregate outputs. The included values and display transformations are inspectable; raw historical return replication is a separate requirement.</dd><dt>Report transcription</dt><dd>A reviewed statement or selected result transcribed from a report. It is not a fresh test or an independently rerun engine.</dd><dt>Executable example</dt><dd>Runnable, independently authored synthetic software. Its tests establish software behavior, not market evidence or historical-code parity.</dd><dt>Private inputs required</dt><dd>Historical-return replication requires omitted private prices, events, execution snapshots or protected ledgers.</dd></dl><h2>Outcomes stay attached to gates</h2><p>Original verdict, normalized status, evidence maturity and reproduction level describe different things. Original verdicts are unavailable for 52 catalog records; a normalized status does not fill that gap.</p><p>A discovery map does not nominate a strategy. An intermediate execution pass does not establish residual alpha. A technically repaired bridge does not certify source rights. Invalid predecessors and corrected versions retain separate records.</p><h2>Missingness and numerical care</h2><p>Nulls stay unavailable. An absent control-row gate field is not false. Four complete trend folds remain separate from the excluded partial fold. Archived annual-percent displays are already converted, and are not multiplied by 100 again.</p><p>No daily trend NAV was persisted. This publication creates no equity curve, underwater plot, rolling Sharpe, new confidence interval, inferred stress point or “best strategy” result.</p><h2>Evidence you can inspect</h2><ul><li><a href="/research/">Six complete research cases</a> link questions to controlling decisions.</li><li><a href="/evidence/claims/">The claim registry</a> preserves all 204 values, caveats and pointers.</li><li><a href="/evidence/sources/">The source index</a> identifies excluded originals and included derivative provenance.</li><li><a href="/methods/">Synthetic method examples</a> are runnable with Python's standard library.</li></ul><h2>Publication scope and rights</h2><p>Only the 110 explicitly mapped reviewed derivatives are downloadable. Source excerpts are separate from those downloads. Permission to cite a source does not grant permission to redistribute its contents. Original complete reports, row-level market data, source engines, TradeX ports, Pine scripts, protected ledgers and the complete handoff archive are excluded.</p><p>Source research declares Proprietary. Reserved rights and material-specific notices remain in force. Read <a href="/publication/">rights and attribution</a> and the <a href="/release/">dated snapshot record</a>.</p></div>
